    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 \u2014 the acceptance suite is the only test class in the project, covering both the soft-delete-and-retain and the deleted-owner-ignored-by-duplicate-check scenarios).\n\n## Summary\n\nOwner deletion is now a soft-delete. Changes, kept small and in low-complexity units to minimize structural impact:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `deleted` boolean to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the flag (MapStruct auto-maps the same-named `Owner.deleted` property; no mapper edits needed).\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `deleted` column field defaulting to `false`, with a plain getter/setter. A newly created owner is therefore `deleted=false`.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.deleteOwner`** \u2014 instead of `deleteOwner(owner)`, it now sets `deleted=true` and saves, retaining the row and returning `204`. GET still finds and returns the owner with `deleted=true`.\n- **`IdentityKey.isDuplicate`** and **`HouseholdMatcher.isHouseholdDuplicate`** \u2014 each now filters out soft-deleted owners before matching. These are the two blocking checks in the create path (their only callers), so a normally-blocking duplicate is allowed when the sole match was deleted. I edited these two small, low-complexity utility methods rather than the complex `addOwner`, so no complex method or class grew.\n- **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** / **`data.sql`** \u2014 added the `deleted BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE` column (test profile) and appended `FALSE` to the positional seed inserts.\n\nI left the `h2`/`postgres`/`mysql` schemas untouched: they already omit several current entity columns (email, postcode, salutation, \u2026) and rely on `ddl-auto`, so hsqldb is the maintained, test-exercised schema and adding the column only there matches the existing pattern.",
